/P 132 0 R
/T (2. Embeddings \(Converting Words into Numbers\) Once text is tokenized, each token is mapped to a dense numerical vector called an embedding. Embeddings place words into a high-dimensional mathematical space where words with similar meanings are located closer together.)
/E (2. Embeddings \(Converting Words into Numbers\) Once text is tokenized, each token is mapped to a dense numerical vector called an embedding. Embeddings place words into a high-dimensional mathematical space where words with similar meanings are located closer together.)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [0]
>>
endobj
170 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/P 461 0 R
/T (Static vs. Contextual Embeddings: Early embedding algorithms like word2vec assigned a single static vector to each word. Modern Language AI uses contextualized embeddings, where the vector representation of a word dynamically changes depending on the surrounding sentence. For instance, the word "bank" receives a different numerical vector in "river bank" versus "investment bank")
/E (Static vs. Contextual Embeddings: Early embedding algorithms like word2vec assigned a single static vector to each word. Modern Language AI uses contextualized embeddings, where the vector representation of a word dynamically changes depending on the surrounding sentence. For instance, the word "bank" receives a different numerical vector in "river bank" versus "investment bank")
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
