/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/P 133 0 R
/T (3. The Transformer Architecture & Self-Attention Most modern Language AI systems rely on the Transformer architecture. The core innovation of the Transformer is the self-attention mechanism, which allows the model to evaluate how every word in a sequence relates to every other word.)
/E (3. The Transformer Architecture & Self-Attention Most modern Language AI systems rely on the Transformer architecture. The core innovation of the Transformer is the self-attention mechanism, which allows the model to evaluate how every word in a sequence relates to every other word.)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [0]
>>
endobj
173 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/P 463 0 R
/T (Example: Consider the prompt: "The dog chased the squirrel because it...". To predict what word comes next, the model must determine what "it" refers to. The self-attention mechanism calculates relevance scores across the tokens and heavily connects "it" to "squirrel" \(or "dog"\), incorporating that context into its final decision.)
/E (Example: Consider the prompt: "The dog chased the squirrel because it...". To predict what word comes next, the model must determine what "it" refers to. The self-attention mechanism calculates relevance scores across the tokens and heavily connects "it" to "squirrel" \(or "dog"\), incorporating that context into its final decision.)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [1]
>>
