/T (The most common method for tokenization is by splitting on a whitespace to create individual words. However, this has its disadvantages as some languages, like Man-darin, do not have whitespaces around individual words. In the next chapter, we will go in depth about tokenization and how that technique influences language models. As illustrated in Figure 1-4, after tokenization, we combine all unique words from each sentence to create a vocabulary that we can use to represent the sentences.)
